spec mg08-merge-vs-delete: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# MG08. s1 DETACH DELETEs the node k='a'; s2, with an older snapshot, runs
# MERGE (n:K {k:'a'}) ON MATCH SET n.v = 1 ON CREATE SET n.v = -1. s2 matches the node
# at its snapshot, and its ON MATCH SET writes a node whose head is not visible to
# it: refused (F2), never written onto a dead node and never resurrected. PostgreSQL
# READ COMMITTED turns the MERGE into an INSERT.

starting permutation: s1d s1c s2m s2c
step s1d: MATCH (n:K {k:'a'}) DETACH DELETE n RETURN count(*) AS deleted
deleted
-------
1      
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2m: MERGE (n:K {k:'a'}) ON MATCH SET n.v = 1 ON CREATE SET n.v = -1 RETURN n.v AS v
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2c: COMMIT
ERROR: cypher: transaction poisoned by a prior failed Exec statement — call Rollback
final final: MATCH (n:K) RETURN n.k AS k, n.v AS v ORDER BY k, v
